---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Brand from '../components/Brand.astro';
import ContactBand from '../components/ContactBand.astro';
import Video from '../components/Video.astro';
---
<Base title="packsel · Less walking. More picking." description="Flexible warehouse automation for 3PLs. Explore packsel mobile robots, see zone picking in action, and estimate the savings for your operation.">
<section class="hero container"><div class="hero-copy stack"><p class="kicker"><span class="signal-dot"></span> Warehouse automation, within reach</p><h1>Less walking.<br>More picking.<br><span class="accent">That’s packsel.</span></h1><p class="lead">Put your people where they add value.<br>Let the robots handle the travel.</p><p class="hero-description"><Brand tm /> brings autonomous mobile robots to 3PL warehouses through a flexible leasing model, built around your operation.</p><div class="cluster"><a class="button button-primary" href="mailto:zach@packsel.co?subject=Warehouse%20automation">Explore your options <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/warehouse-demo/">See the warehouse demo <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div><figure class="hero-visual"><img src="/images/warehouse-robots.webp" srcset="/images/warehouse-robots-800.webp 800w, /images/warehouse-robots.webp 1440w" sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 55vw" alt="packsel shelf robots carrying separate totes through a warehouse aisle" width="1440" height="960" fetchpriority="high" /><figcaption><span>Built for the work between picks.</span><span>Product visualization</span></figcaption></figure></section>
<div class="container"><div class="capability-rail"><span>Designed around your floor</span><span>Robots as a service</span><span>People + automation</span><a href="/how-it-works/">From assessment to operation ↗</a></div></div>
<section class="section-large container"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="kicker">A better division of labor</p><h2>Your people do the picking.<br>Your robots do the moving.</h2></div><p class="lead">A warehouse works better when every trip has a purpose. Bring orders to your associates, then move completed picks to packing.</p></div><div class="workflow-row">{[{n:'01',title:'Bring work to the zone',body:'AMRs travel between picking zones while associates stay close to the inventory they know.'},{n:'02',title:'Keep orders organized',body:'Separate bins and scan-guided workflows help associates put each item in the right order.'},{n:'03',title:'Keep fulfillment moving',body:'Robots carry picked orders to packing and return for the next assignment.'}].map(x=><article class="workflow-item"><span class="mono step-number">{x.n}</span><h3>{x.title}</h3><p>{x.body}</p></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="surface-sunken section-large"><div class="container product-feature"><div class="product-plate"><span class="kicker plate-label">Meet your next workhorse</span><img src="/images/transport-robot.webp" alt="packsel transport robot with a compact base, upright mast, and touchscreen" width="800" height="1200" loading="lazy" /><span class="mono plate-caption">Product visualization · configuration varies</span></div><div class="stack product-copy"><p class="kicker">Practical robots. Real work.</p><h2>A small footprint.<br>A bigger role on<br>your warehouse floor.</h2><p class="lead">From moving materials to supporting multi-order picking, start with the configuration your workflow needs.</p><div class="feature-lines"><div><span class="mono">01</span><p><strong>Compact mobile base</strong><br>Built to move through working environments.</p></div><div><span class="mono">02</span><p><strong>Flexible carrying options</strong><br>Platform and shelf configurations for different loads.</p></div><div><span class="mono">03</span><p><strong>Onboard touchscreen</strong><br>A clear point of interaction on the floor.</p></div></div><a class="text-link" href="/robots/">Explore the robots <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div></section>
<section class="section-large container"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="kicker">Step inside the workflow</p><h2>See your warehouse<br>in a different way.</h2></div><div class="stack"><p class="lead">Follow an AMR from order assignment to the packing station. Explore the zones, people, and routes that bring it together.</p><a class="text-link" href="/warehouse-demo/">Launch the interactive demo →</a></div></div><a class="demo-preview" href="/warehouse-demo/" aria-label="Launch the interactive 3D warehouse demo"><img src="/images/warehouse-demo.webp" alt="Overview of the interactive warehouse with rack aisles, zone pickers, and mobile robots" width="1440" height="840" loading="lazy" /><span class="demo-preview-bar"><span><span class="signal-dot"></span> An illustrative zone-picking operation</span><span class="button button-primary">Explore in 3D ↗</span></span></a></section>
<section class="savings-teaser section-large"><div class="container split"><div class="stack"><p class="kicker">Build your business case</p><h2>What could less<br>walking be worth?</h2><p class="lead">Start with your team, wages, and operating hours. Adjust the assumptions and see how robot costs compare with the value of time saved.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/savings/">Estimate your savings ↗</a></div><div class="calculator-illustration" aria-label="Calculator inputs include workforce, wages, efficiency, and robot costs"><div class="mini-heading"><span class="mono">Your operation. Your assumptions.</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>{[{label:'Employees in the workflow',width:'64%'},{label:'Average hourly wage',width:'42%'},{label:'Labor hours saved',width:'30%'}].map(x=><div class="mini-slider"><span>{x.label}</span><div><i style={`width:${x.width}`}></i></div></div>)}<div class="mini-result"><span>Explore monthly & annual impact</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section-large container split video-section"><div class="stack"><p class="kicker">From concept to movement</p><h2>Watch the hardware<br>get to work.</h2><p class="lead">Take a closer look at the robot platform in motion and the material-handling tasks it can support.</p><p class="small secondary">The video shows the robot platform. Your final workflow and configuration are defined during assessment.</p></div><Video /></section>
<section class="section-large container faq-section"><div><p class="kicker">A few good questions</p><h2>Before your<br>first robot.</h2></div><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Is this designed for 3PLs?</summary><p>Yes. We focus on the picking and transport challenges of small and mid-size warehouses, including 3PL operations with multiple clients and changing order volumes.</p></details><details><summary>Do we need to buy the robots?</summary><p>packsel’s model is leasing. Fleet size, term, implementation, and support scope are defined in your proposal after we review your operation.</p></details><details><summary>Can this work with our WMS?</summary><p>We assess your warehouse management system’s API, order data, item locations, and scanning requirements before defining an integration. Compatibility needs to be confirmed for your system.</p></details><details><summary>How much could we save?</summary><p>That depends on your labor costs, travel time, order profile, and fleet requirements. Our calculator is a starting point for scenarios, followed by a workflow assessment.</p></details></div></section>
<ContactBand />
</Base>
